                <pb facs="0158" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg74"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-08-17"><hi rendition="#italic">August 17,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1370.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm your telegram
                    of August 15.</p>
                <p>I have made it perfectly clear to Prince Ch’ing that the date for signing of the
                    completed treaty, October 8, is absolute and not contingent on any action of
                    Russia.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
